   "notes": "The medium is fully defined in the paper's 'Culture medium' section and is already complete at the ionic level: the current exchange list (Cl, glycerol, K, Mg, Na, NH4, O2, Pi, SO4) captures every species contributed by the five salts plus the N and C sources. N−C− minimal medium (Csonka/Kustu) is a phosphate-buffered defined salts medium that intentionally contains NO added trace-metal/micronutrient mix, NO CaCl2, and NO vitamins/thiamine — verified by convergent reproduction of the identical recipe in independent papers; growth relies on trace-metal contaminants. 1 mM IPTG was added 'when ne"
